  "Born George Samuel Schuyler in Providence, Rhode Island, on 25 February 1895; he served in the army, worked as a journalist for the Pittsburgh Courier and The Messenger, and published Black No More in 1931, followed by Slaves Today (1931) and Black and Conservative (1966). He died in New York on 31 August 1977.",
